; WILDCARD_FALSE_POSITIVE — the fixture that stops us shipping a verifier which
; marks unconfigured domains as verified.
;
; A wildcard answers for every name, so a naive "did the lookup return
; something?" check passes for a customer who added nothing at all. Detection
; here is behavioural: probe a random label, and if that answers too, the
; specific record was never added.
;
; The signed counterpart (zones/src/wildcard-signed.test.zone) covers the other
; detection path — RRSIG Labels being smaller than the answer owner's label
; count, which is an authoritative signal rather than a probe. Both paths need
; their own fixture or one of them ships untested.
$ORIGIN wildcard.test.
$TTL 60

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 60 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.

*       IN TXT  "wildcard-synthesized-do-not-trust"
*       IN A    198.51.100.30

; A genuinely configured name alongside the wildcard, so wildcard detection can
; be shown not to produce a false *negative* when the real record also exists.
_propgate-verify    IN TXT  "propgate-site-verification=fixture-abc123"
